---
import DocShell from '../layouts/doc-shell.astro';
import { docsLinks } from '../lib/nav';
---

<DocShell
   title="CLI reference"
   summary="Complete command reference for the a11ied CLI. Each command family handles one part of the accessibility testing workflow."
   links={docsLinks}
>
   <section class="ledger">
      <div class="panel-head">
         <p class="panel-kicker">Command map</p>
         <h2>Command families</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="route-list">
         <div class="route-row"><code>wcag</code><span>Look up criteria, levels, search results, and coverage strategy.</span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><code>inspect</code><span>Check which criteria apply to a page or Storybook story.</span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><code>drive</code><span>Control a screen reader session with low-level actions.</span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><code>doctor</code><span>Report target availability and recording diagnostics.</span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><code>run</code><span>Execute <code>axe-core</code> scans or named interaction patterns.</span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><code>verify</code><span>Produce criterion or level verdicts from collected evidence.</span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><code>mcp</code><span>Start the stdio MCP server.</span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><code>help-all</code><span>Print the entire command tree in one shot — useful for agents discovering the CLI.</span></div>
      </div>
   </section>

   <section class="panel">
      <div class="panel-head">
         <p class="panel-kicker">Subcommands</p>
         <h2>Subcommands by family</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="mini-grid">
         <div class="stack">
            <h3>wcag</h3>
            <p><code>levels</code>, <code>criteria</code>, <code>show</code>, <code>search</code>, <code>coverage</code></p>
         </div>
         <div class="stack">
            <h3>inspect</h3>
            <p><code>applicable</code>, <code>criterion</code></p>
         </div>
         <div class="stack">
            <h3>drive</h3>
            <p><code>start</code>, <code>status</code>, <code>stop</code>, plus <code>next</code>, <code>key</code>, <code>read</code>, <code>logs</code></p>
         </div>
         <div class="stack">
            <h3>run</h3>
            <p><code>axe</code> and <code>pattern</code></p>
         </div>
         <div class="stack">
            <h3>verify</h3>
            <p><code>criterion</code> and <code>level</code></p>
         </div>
      </div>
   </section>

   <section class="split panel">
      <div class="stack">
         <div class="panel-head">
            <p class="panel-kicker">Example</p>
            <h2>One criterion, end to end</h2>
         </div>
      <pre><code>node packages/cli/dist/cli.js wcag show 4.1.3 --json
node packages/cli/dist/cli.js inspect criterion 4.1.3 --url http://127.0.0.1:6173/status-message.html --json
node packages/cli/dist/cli.js run pattern status_message_probe --target virtual --url http://127.0.0.1:6173/status-message.html --json
node packages/cli/dist/cli.js verify criterion 4.1.3 --target virtual --url http://127.0.0.1:6173/status-message.html --json</code></pre>
      <p>
         This sequence runs through all four steps: lookup, applicability check, evidence gathering,
         and verification.
      </p>
      </div>
      <div class="split-aside">
         <div class="tag">see also</div>
         <p class="aside-note">
            For guided walkthroughs, see <a href="/workflows">workflows</a>.
         </p>
      </div>
   </section>

   <section class="panel">
      <div class="panel-head">
         <p class="panel-kicker">Agent support</p>
         <h2>Print the full command tree</h2>
      </div>
      <pre><code>node packages/cli/dist/cli.js help-all</code></pre>
      <p>
         Outputs every subcommand and flag in one pass. Useful for AI agents exploring the CLI
         surface programmatically.
      </p>
   </section>

   <section class="field-note">
      <div class="panel-head">
         <p class="panel-kicker">Tip</p>
         <h2>Start with the smallest command</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
         If you only need criterion text, use <code>wcag show</code> — no browser required. The CLI
         is layered so you can pick the right level of effort for each task.
      </p>
   </section>
</DocShell>
